      <description>&lt;aside class=&#34;clanker-note&#34; style=&#34;border-left: 3px solid #999; padding: 0.4em 0.9em; margin: 1em 0; font-size: 0.92em; color: #555;&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p style=&#34;margin: 0;&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How this post was written:&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;  the experience, the work and the decisions are mine. I used a clanker (a coding agent) to turn my notes, commits and memories into a cohesive story, then reviewed it for accuracy. See &lt;a href=&#34;http://niteria.github.io/posts/why-its-frustrating-to-work-with-clankers/&#34;&gt;my series on working with clankers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/aside&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Four years after &lt;a href=&#34;http://niteria.github.io/posts/the-compiler-is-wrong/&#34;&gt;the compiler was wrong&lt;/a&gt;, almost to the day, it was glibc.&#xA;And glibc had already fixed it, four years earlier.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
